												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“We want to release in Early Acess for Bruisers 2d, as the core gameplay has remained the focus for about 7 years, with it finally feeling polished and great to play. I believe the game is ready for the public to experience, with the opportunity to shape the career mode further. <br />
<br />
Early Access allows us to refine fight mechanics, AI behaviour, and career progression based on how people actually play, rather than relying solely on internal testing. We also plan to expand content during this period, including additional fighters, events, and features.<br />
<br />
Our goal is to work closely with players to shape Bruisers into a deep, rewarding boxing experience that holds up over long careers, not just short play sessions.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“2 years will be the goal to polish it to it's final state, to finally call it finished. ”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“We plan to expand on the career mode, with further story beats in the pro mode. We plan to hone in on the amateur stage of the career mode further, by adding competitions/olympic style presentation/tournament etc. Also further expand the bareknuckle career with challenges and story beats. Also further polishing the customisation options, to allow more options with a better presentation.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The in ring gameplay is polished to an almost finished standard, with some further enhancements to be expected. Like customisation/balancing/feature additions if neccessary. The career mode is about 70% finished, with it being fully playable, but needing some further details to feel immersive to the intended level.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“We plan to gradually raise the price as we ship new content and features. Entirely dependent on how much content is added along the way.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We have an open discussion policy, where the dev is constantly answering questions and looking for suggestions from the community there. Also being active in youtube comments and the steam page community discussion board.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
